; diag-dur-unbound: referencing `dur` in an expr when the transport
; declares no :dur is an UnknownBinding at the load-time dry-run — the
; single code path Compile and Eval share, so what the dry-run rejects
; the frame never reaches. Pins the expr_eval_failed diagnostic and its
; span: the compile-time guard for the optional dur binding.
(transport :bpm 120 :meter [4 4])

(track :target span :expr (* dur 2))
